<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Piedra del Aguila gets $100 mln loan.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Piedra del Aguila gets $100 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine hydroelectric dam Piedra del Aguila Monday said it signed a $100 million syndicated loan deal in which The First National Bank of Boston and local Banco Rio de la Plata will act as managers.</p>
<p>The three-year loan carries an 8.75 percent annual interest rate, Piedra del Aguila told the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Proceeds will be applied to cancel an $80 million syndicated loan signed in May last year and to refinance other liabilities.</p>
<p>Piedra del Aguila is controlled by a group formed by Chile's Chilgener SA, Canada's Transalta Corp and U.S. company Duke Power.</p>
<p>((--Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
